<section class="section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="section-label">Common questions</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Straight answers.</h2>
    <div class="web-faq-list">
      <div class="web-faq-item">
        <div class="web-faq-q">Is it really $100?</div>
        <div class="web-faq-a">Yes. One-time payment. No hidden fees. No monthly charges. The site is yours.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="web-faq-item">
        <div class="web-faq-q">What if I need changes later?</div>
        <div class="web-faq-a">Minor text and photo updates are free for 30 days after launch. After that, changes are $25/hour — usually 15-30 minutes of work.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="web-faq-item">
        <div class="web-faq-q">Do I need to provide content?</div>
        <div class="web-faq-a">I'll pull from your Google Business Profile and any existing materials. If you have photos, great. If not, I'll use high-quality stock images that fit your industry.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="web-faq-item">
        <div class="web-faq-q">What platform is it built on?</div>
        <div class="web-faq-a">Depends on your needs. Most sites are built as lightweight static HTML/CSS for speed and simplicity. Some use Manus for more complex features like booking forms or before/after sliders.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="web-faq-item">
        <div class="web-faq-q">Can you help with SEO after launch?</div>
        <div class="web-faq-a">Yes — that's a separate service. See my <a href="/marketing" style="color: var(--terra);">marketing services</a> for ongoing SEO, local search, and paid ads management.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="web-faq-item">
        <div class="web-faq-q">What if my business isn't a good fit?</div>
        <div class="web-faq-a">I'll tell you upfront. The $100 website is designed for service businesses — home services, health and wellness, professional services, trades, etc. If your needs are more complex, I'll recommend a different approach.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

